.TH AUTOBDP 1 "September 2026" "v1.1" "AutoBDP Manual"
.SH NAME
AutoBDP \- Automated Binary Decompiler Pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B AutoBDP
.br
.B AutoBDP \-\-headless
.br
.B AutoBDP \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AutoBDP
is an automated reverse-engineering framework that transforms raw compiled executables into functionally equivalent, compilable source code. It integrates headless static extraction, AI-driven code synthesis, smart self-healing compilation, and dynamic behavioral verification.

By default, executing 
.B AutoBDP
without arguments launches the interactive Graphical User Interface (GUI). For terminal environments or automated workflows, the 
.B \-\-headless
flag initiates the command-line interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B (no options)
Starts the Graphical User Interface (GUI) for interactive binary analysis.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Starts the command-line interface (CLI) version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Displays the help menu and exits.
.SH PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE
.TP
.B 1. Headless Static Extraction
Utilizes Ghidra in headless mode to extract pseudo-C, synchronized assembly listings, and read-only memory maps from the target executable.
.TP
.B 2. Context-Aware LLM Synthesis
Feeds the extracted context to the Gemini API to reconstruct standard, idiomatically correct source code.
.TP
.B 3. Smart Compilation & Self-Healing Loop
Analyzes the synthesized code to dynamically query the AI for the appropriate compiler (e.g., \fBgcc\fR, \fBg++\fR, \fBclang\fR) and necessary linker flags (e.g., \fB-lm\fR, \fB-lpthread\fR). If compilation fails, the intercepted error diagnostics (\fBstderr\fR) are fed back to the LLM for iterative patching until a clean build is achieved.
.TP
.B 4. Dynamic Behavioral Verification
Executes both the original and synthesized binaries inside an \fBstrace\fR wrapper. The resulting system call traces are normalized and diffed to guarantee 100% runtime execution equivalence.
